    "created_at": "2016-03-17T13:17:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-17T13:17:22Z",
    "body": "@jonco3 `document.open()` replaces the Window object, while leaving the Document object unchanged. A test would then show that your implementation is different from what Domenic is proposing. I tend to agree though that storing it on the Document object is better, since that is where we have stored most stuff thus far and that works better with history, which does not have a Window.\n",
